Place @eggplant{1%medium}(cut into 1-inch cubes) in a #colander{}, sprinkle with @salt{1%teaspoon} and let drain in the sink or over a #bowl{} while prepping the remaining vegetables.

Pat the eggplant dry with a paper towel.

Heat 2 tablespoons @olive oil{1/4%cup}(divided) over medium-high heat in a #Dutch oven{}. Add the eggplant, reduce to medium heat and cook ~{3-4%minutes} or until beginning to soften and is lightly browned. Transfer to a bowl.

Refresh oil as needed. Add @zucchini{2%medium}(cut into 1-inch pieces) and @yellow squash{2%medium}(cut into 1-inch pieces) and cook ~{3-4%minutes} or until beginning to soften and is lightly browned. Transfer to the bowl with the eggplant.

Refresh oil if needed. Add the @red onion{1%medium}(cut into 1/2-inch pieces) and cook ~{4-5%minutes} or until the onions begin to soften, adjusting the heat as necessary so the onions don't burn.

Add the @red or yellow bell peppers{2}(cut into 1/2-inch pieces) and continue cooking another ~{3-4%minutes} or until beginning to soften.

Add @plum tomatoes{3%large}(seeded and coarsely chopped) and @garlic{4%cloves}(minced) and cook ~{1-2%minutes}.

Add @dry white wine{1/2%cup}, bring to a boil and cook ~{1-2%minutes}.

Add @crushed tomatoes{1%15-ounce can}, @bay leaf{1}, @dried oregano{1%heaping teaspoon} and @crushed red pepper flakes{1/2%teaspoon}.

Return eggplant, zucchini and yellow squash to the pot, reduce heat to medium-low and simmer uncovered ~{20-25%minutes} or until vegetables are tender.

Season with @salt{} and @freshly ground black pepper{} to taste. Remove bay leaf. Stir in @fresh basil{1/4%cup}(thinly sliced).